WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.633
Confirming a guess is far easier than naming the
exact class.

00:00:03.713 --> 00:00:07.346
If an expert only answers a binary yes-or-no question,

00:00:07.426 --> 00:00:11.059
the labeling cost per node drops sharply,
especially with many classes.

00:00:11.139 --> 00:00:14.771
Meanwhile,

00:00:14.851 --> 00:00:18.484
existing selection criteria were built for hard
labels and only measure a single node's uncertainty.

00:00:18.564 --> 00:00:22.197
They ignore that in a graph network,

00:00:22.277 --> 00:00:25.910
labeling one node propagates supervision across its
k-hop neighborhood.
